{"id": "EUVD-2026-71513", "enisaUuid": "689e7b1c-6cc1-33fd-ac76-3afdd6132b7b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/tegra: gr2d/gr3d: Initialize address register map before HOST1X client is registered\n\nThe host1x_client_register() function is called just prior to register map\ninitialization loop, making the device available to userspace. This may\nresult in userspace attempting to submits a job before the register map is\ninitialized. Address this by moving register initialization before host1x\nclient registration.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T16:49:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-07T14:21:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e22d5ad61cfa38aa53fab86a530113aff6a3619", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5db37fd7710e74bc4df48bddab8f571d0bfc6769", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40a2a91da02c434938f0ba53877984820800b5f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3055292b8eed69553b389a609197a241df47e68e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4ef5ba1131346159e31f4ef858525cf377380a6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-924c-v8fr-v5mq", "CVE-2026-80883"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1cbc7398-3b7d-300f-8759-f7ffa91b8d5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.10"}, {"id": "2c798843-82d6-3240-89d0-d94407a7222d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "36ec61bd-2f1c-30f3-93ec-efe1781845ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d43f81cbaf43531a977e8b4c4427f19acf8a5061 <3055292b8eed69553b389a609197a241df47e68e"}, {"id": "3ed5fab0-9e1b-31f0-840c-73ff90ef0856", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d43f81cbaf43531a977e8b4c4427f19acf8a5061 <c4ef5ba1131346159e31f4ef858525cf377380a6"}, {"id": "4241671f-ec34-3baf-b44f-2335081cc21a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ve